  ($qb$S20C07Q08$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The organisation's track record of releasing approved transformation budgets on time in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — approved budgets are released as planned$qb$, $qb$Generally reliable — budgets are released with minor delays$qb$, $qb$Inconsistent — budget release timing is unpredictable$qb$, $qb$Poor — budget release delays have historically undermined transformation execution$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C07Q09$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The degree to which transformation ROI is tracked and reported in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Rigorously — all transformation investment is tracked against defined outcomes and reported to leadership$qb$, $qb$Generally tracked — major transformation investments are tracked$qb$, $qb$Partially tracked — some tracking occurs without comprehensive coverage$qb$, $qb$Not tracked — transformation investment is not tracked against outcomes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C07Q10$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Overall, investment readiness for transformation in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Is strong — the organisation is financially ready to invest in the transformation it needs$qb$, $qb$Is adequate — the necessary investment is feasible with appropriate prioritisation$qb$, $qb$Is constrained — financial limitations would significantly impact the scale or pace of transformation$qb$, $qb$Is a critical barrier — insufficient investment readiness would prevent meaningful transformation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q01$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The number of significant transformation programmes the organisation has run in the last 5 years is:$qb$, $qb$More than 3 — the organisation is experienced in managing multiple transformation waves$qb$, $qb$2-3 — the organisation has recent, relevant transformation experience$qb$, $qb$1 — the organisation has some recent transformation experience to build on$qb$, $qb$None — this would be the organisation's first significant transformation programme$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q02$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The success rate of previous transformation programmes in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$High — most transformations have achieved their primary objectives$qb$, $qb$Generally positive — transformations have mostly achieved what they set out to do$qb$, $qb$Mixed — some have succeeded; others have significantly underperformed$qb$, $qb$Poor — previous transformations have largely not achieved their stated objectives$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
